### ============================================================================
### CASO C-02: Autorregistro de clientes (RN-02)
### ============================================================================

### 1. Registro exitoso -> 201 Created
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/registro
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "esteban_cliente@test.com",
  "nombre": "Esteban Cliente",
  "password": "PasswordSegura123!",
  "documento": "34567890",
  "telefono": "1144332211"
}

### 2. Intento de registro con correo duplicado -> 409 Conflict
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/registro
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "cliente@example.com",
  "nombre": "Duplicado Correo",
  "password": "PasswordSegura123!",
  "documento": "99999999",
  "telefono": "1144332211"
}

### 3. Intento de registro con documento duplicado -> 409 Conflict
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/registro
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nuevo_doc_dup@test.com",
  "nombre": "Duplicado Doc",
  "password": "PasswordSegura123!",
  "documento": "30111222",
  "telefono": "1144332211"
}


### ============================================================================
### CASO C-03: Login y Cookie de Sesión HttpOnly (RN-03)
### ============================================================================

# @name loginAdmin
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Consultar perfil con sesión iniciada
GET http://localhost:8000/auth/yo
Accept: application/json

### Intentar acceder a ruta protegida sin cookie o con Authorization: Bearer -> 401 Unauthorized
# @no-cookie-jar
GET http://localhost:8000/repuestos
Authorization: Bearer un-token-invalido-que-no-debe-usarse
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================================
### CASO C-04: Credenciales inválidas y tiempo constante (RN-09)
### ============================================================================

### Correo existente con contraseña errónea -> 401 Credenciales inválidas
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "ContraseñaIncorrecta"
}

### Correo inexistente -> 401 Credenciales inválidas (mismo mensaje y tiempo)
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "correo_inexistente_999@test.com",
  "password": "ContraseñaIncorrecta"
}


### ============================================================================
### CASO C-09: Cambio obligatorio de contraseña
### ============================================================================

# @name loginNuevo
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nuevo@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Intento de acceder a repuestos con cambio obligatorio pendiente -> 403 Forbidden
GET http://localhost:8000/repuestos
Accept: application/json

### Cambio de contraseña exitoso -> 200 OK y cookie renovada
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/cambiar-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password_actual": "Password123!",
  "password_nueva": "MiNuevaPassword456!"
}

### Reintento de acceso a repuestos tras el cambio -> 200 OK
GET http://localhost:8000/repuestos
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================================
### Cierre de sesión (Logout)
### ============================================================================

POST http://localhost:8000/auth/logout
